Source: uv
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Dario Griffo <dariogriffo@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), wget, ca-certificates
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/astral-sh/uv
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: uv
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armel armhf ppc64el s390x riscv64 i386
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: An extremely fast Python package and project manager, written in Rust
 uv is an extremely fast Python package installer and resolver, written in Rust,
 and designed as a drop-in replacement for pip and pip-tools workflows.
 .
 This package also installs uvx, the uv tool runner, which runs a command
 provided by a Python package in a temporary, isolated environment.

Package: uvx
Architecture: all
Depends: uv (>= ${source:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Run tools published as Python packages, without installing them
 uvx runs a command provided by a Python package in a temporary, isolated
 environment, similar to pipx run. It is the tool runner of uv and is an
 alias for "uv tool run".
 .
 The uvx executable itself is shipped by the uv package as /usr/bin/uvx,
 because uvx is a small trampoline that looks for the uv binary sitting next
 to it and cannot run without it. This package installs no files of its own;
 it exists so that "apt install uvx" and "apt search uvx" lead to uv.
